  "conclusion": "At 8 RPS with ISL17/OSL32, approximately one two-second slow SSE consumer at a time increased healthy TTFT P95 by 0.572 ms and healthy E2E P95 by 3.804 ms on paired means; 339/339 healthy treatment requests met both SLOs and every request, terminal, and tracked resource converged.",
